      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\int (6{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (6{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-3\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
